# Security rules

## Doc map

- **Setup & commands** → [README.md](../../README.md)
- **System design & deployment** → [ARCHITECTURE.md](../../ARCHITECTURE.md)
- **Stack, paths & conventions** → [PROJECT.md](../../PROJECT.md)

## Secrets & credentials

- Never commit secrets, API keys, tokens, or credentials. Use env vars and GitHub Actions secrets.
- Do not log PII or session tokens to `console.*`.

## XSS prevention

- No `innerHTML` / `outerHTML` for user-facing KNM content — use text nodes.
- If HTML injection is ever required, sanitize with DOMPurify and document why.
- Do not construct URLs or `href`/`src` from unvalidated user input without encoding.
- Avoid dynamic code evaluation and injected script tags.

## Content Security Policy

- Prefer Tailwind/CSS classes over inline `style` with user-supplied values.

## Network

- This site is static; question data is bundled at build time — no runtime public API by default.
- Any future `fetch` to external APIs: validate responses at the boundary; encode URL segments with `encodeURIComponent`.
- Do not use `mode: "no-cors"` on fetch — it hides errors.

## Deploy secrets

- Bunny CDN credentials only in CI secrets or local env — never in source. See ARCHITECTURE.md.

## Input validation

- Validate at boundaries: locale handoff JSON in `sessionStorage`, any future form input.
- Never trust external API shapes without validation.

## Dependency hygiene

- Run `npm audit` before releases; address high/critical findings.
- Avoid unmaintained packages without justification.

## Legal & privacy copy

- **Always ask before editing** `src/i18n/legal.ts` or legal pages under `src/pages/`.
- Do not weaken consent, disclosure, or opt-out language.
